---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Dynamic for the same reason as terms.astro: BaseLayout's nav/footer read
// per-request session and locale state. Policy terms confirmed by the owner
// on 25 September 2026 (required page for Razorpay card-network activation).
export const prerender = false;

const lastUpdated = '27 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cancellation & Refund Policy — IWIS Global"
  description="How cancellations, refunds, and date changes work for IWIS Global tours: full refund up to 24 hours before, refund timelines, and what happens if we cancel."
>
  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-serif font-semibold mb-1">Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mb-6">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      This policy applies to every tour booked on this website with IWIS Global ("we", "us"). All times
      are India Standard Time (IST), measured from your tour's scheduled start time.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">If you cancel</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-3">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-stone-300 text-left">
            <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">When you cancel</th>
            <th class="py-2 font-semibold">Refund</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-stone-700">
          <tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">24 hours or more before the tour starts</td>
            <td class="py-2"><strong>100%</strong> of the amount you've paid</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">Less than 24 hours before the tour starts</td>
            <td class="py-2"><strong>50%</strong> of the amount you've paid</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">No-show (you don't arrive for pickup and haven't cancelled)</td>
            <td class="py-2">No refund</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      If you paid a 25% deposit, the refund is calculated on the deposit you paid; the balance is only
      due at pickup, so nothing more is owed after a cancellation.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">How to cancel</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      Email <a href="mailto:info@iwisglobal.com" class="text-brand-800 hover:underline">info@iwisglobal.com</a> or
      message us on
      <a href={`https://wa.me/916399226633?text=${encodeURIComponent("Hi! I'd like to cancel a booking. (ref: REFUND-POLICY)")}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-wa-ref="REFUND-POLICY" class="text-brand-800 hover:underline">WhatsApp (+91 6399226633)</a>
      with your name and the booking ID from your confirmation email (or the payment reference in
      <a href="/account/bookings" class="text-brand-800 hover:underline">My Bookings</a>).
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">If we cancel</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      Occasionally a tour can't run as planned — for example an unscheduled monument closure, severe weather,
      a strike, or a vehicle problem. If we have to cancel, you choose: a <strong>full refund</strong> of
      everything you've paid, or a <strong>free change to a new date</strong>. The Taj Mahal's regular Friday
      closure isn't a cancellation, because tours can't be booked for a Friday in the first place.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Changing your tour date</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      You can move your tour to a different date free of charge up to 24 hours before it starts, subject to
      availability. If the new date or a change in group size costs more, you pay the difference. Date changes
      requested less than 24 hours before the tour are treated as a late cancellation.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Refund timeline</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-stone-700 space-y-1 mb-6">
      <li>We initiate approved refunds within <strong>2 business days</strong>.</li>
      <li>Refunds go back to the <strong>original payment method</strong> through our payment processor, Razorpay.</li>
      <li>Your bank or card issuer usually credits the amount within <strong>7–10 business days</strong> of it being initiated (Razorpay's standard timeline for refunds).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Questions</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700">
      See also our <a href="/terms" class="text-brand-800 hover:underline">Terms of Service</a>, or
      <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-800 hover:underline">contact us</a> about a specific booking.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
